A||||2||jeffozz||Post Swap Meet Info Forwarded (from Ed Parks)||||1||
Z||000000||jeffozz||05-01-2001||12:21 AM||||"List friends, well, the 3rd Annual (maybe last) All Fiero Flea Market and<BR>Swap Meet is over for this year. Seems like everyone wants a 4th Annual<BR>(maybe last) next year, so, it too will be the last weekend of Apr, 02. <P>Didn't see anything but smiling faces (this is the good), so would guess<BR>everyone had a fun time. I certainly did.<P>Lots of folks wanted to know:...how many? So....there were nearly 250<BR>hotdogs/chili dogs eaten, almost 16 cases of cold<BR>drinks/water.......OPPS, those are the wrong numbers! <P>Actually, 188 folks registered and they came from 26 different states.<BR>Last year 151 registered and they also came from 26 different states.<BR>Mike Mohr (Nebraska), Fred Clarke (R.I), Paul Vargas, Ill (our deepest<BR>condolences) and one couple who broke down before they even got out of<BR>Calif, couldn't make it (none of those states were represented), or the<BR>old record would have been broken. Missed you folks.<P>We owe many thanks to all the volunteers who manned (womanned?) the<BR>registration/raffle tables, the kitchen, and handled the tee shirts. As<BR>well as everyone (the same ones plus lots more) who turned out the week<BR>before for cleaning and clearing a place for the Swap Meet to be set up.<P>Can't think of everyone, but special thanks to Jeff (painting & pushing)<BR>and Susie (even cleaning glass with a razor blade) who came a week early<BR>from Detroit, Rick (relocated the walls and organized the fun run), our<BR>son John (who also came in early to push/tote), Ed (on the floors all<BR>week because we kept getting them dirty) and Bev (in the kitchen), Pat<BR>(was her chili good or what??), Jason and Danny (bush hogged with their<BR>own equipment or the weeds would have been taller then the tents!), David<BR>and Kimberly (designed, paid for, and brought the tee shirts up), and the<BR>Fiero Factory staff (Dave, Jeremy, and Rik) who ARE the Fiero Factory and<BR>worked through a lot of the fun. <P>There were so many others.<P>More thanks go for the donated GREAT prizes for the raffles and equally<BR>good value grab bags, the "professional" vendors..Rodney Dickman...Bob &<BR>Lyn Englert...Paul McKibben...Darrell Morse...Dave Held...Dave<BR>Kauzlarich...as well as the MANY folks that brought LOT'S of good used<BR>parts from everywhere. All helped to make this a uniquely good time.<P>Now... the bad. We apologize to any that were not given a brief<BR>instruction sheet that outlined the raffle time and asked to sign The<BR>Wall.. Thats what happens when you can't get good help!!!!!!<P>Also, during the last several days, we have gotten VERY far behind in<BR>answering email and we also apologize for that. We should be able to<BR>catch up soon.<P>Regardless of the "snags", thanks to everyone who came, put a face to<BR>their email or the voice on the phone, and MADE this the best Swap Meet<BR>we have had the pleasure to host.<P>Fiero Folks are the Finest.<P>Again, would someone post this to the lists/forums we are not on, which<BR>is every one except Wallaces' Yahoo list. Thanks<P>Ed Parks...from: The Fiero Factory<BR>8710B Hwy 53<BR>Toney, Ala 35773<BR>Days: 256-420-5391   Nights 256-882-1568 <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory"" TARGET=_blank>http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory"</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||05-01-2001||07:40 AM||||What a nice post. Although I've never met him, Ed sounds like a first class person. His willingness to help all who ask is a fine example of how to build a good small business. By word-of-mouth, news of his superior customer service has truly turned him into and icon of the Fiero community.<P>I wish I cold have attended but I had family come in from North Carolina and a wedding to attend on Saturday. Sounds like I'll have another chance next year. Sounds like it's becoming as big as Daytona.<P>Thanks for the pictures and updates from all who attended,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||85Josh||05-01-2001||01:35 PM||||Ed is clearly a class act. If you think about it, he allowed his COMPETITION to use his place of buisiness, which he closed, and then spent the weekend diagnosing problems and dispensing advice! I think the only thing I saw him sell was his decarbonizing kit, which I can personally say works great! Thanks, Ed!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||14
